      en: "Al-Gurgi Madrasa in Tripoli was founded in 1830 by Mustafa Gurgi. It features a central courtyard, prayer hall, and student cells. Walls are adorned with colorful tiles. It served as a center for Islamic learning. Restored in the 20th century, it is now a tourist attraction. The architecture blends Ottoman and Moorish styles.",
