      en: "The Susa Archaeological Museum is located in the city of Susa, near the ancient Greek colony of Cyrene. Established in 1990, the museum features artifacts from the Cyrenaica region spanning Greek, Roman, and Byzantine periods. Its collection includes pottery, coins, sculptures, and mosaics. Notable exhibits include a marble statue of Apollo and a collection of ancient Greek inscriptions. The museum has 5 galleries and a research library. It underwent a renovation in 2008 funded by the EU. Annual visitation is about 25,000.",
