      en: "The Conference Palace of Sirte is a large convention center located in the coastal city of Sirte, Libya. Opened in 2008, it was designed to host African Union summits and other international meetings. The palace covers 50,000 square meters and features a main auditorium with 2,000 seats, multiple conference rooms, and a press center. Its modern design incorporates glass and steel. The building was damaged during the 2011 civil war but underwent partial restoration by 2015. It currently serves as a venue for cultural events and political gatherings.",
